          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "6bb65cda-48c7-59fd-9810-2d890c6f1d2d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1139,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.45.030:block:1",
          "start": 475
        },
        "quote": "(b) If the lots for which building permits are being requested are located in such a manner that access to the nearest existing public improvement is restricted by a separation of ownership and subdivision but having a continuity of dedicated right-of-way, then such connecting public improvements shall not be subject to the provisions of County Resolution No. 77-255. However, the owner of the lots requesting a building permit shall be required to make such improvements as requested by the County Engineer; provided, however, all lots abutting on an existing County road, as determined by the County Engineer, shall be exempt from County Resolution No. 77-255.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.45.030:block:1#text",
